BRD – Action 1: Google sign‑up / sign‑in
Business goal:

As a user, I can:

Click “Continue with Google” on Sign Up to create an account using my Google email.

Click “Sign in with Google” on Sign In to log in without entering a password.

If my Google email already exists in the system (created earlier with normal signup), the app should link my Google login to the same account instead of creating a duplicate.

If I use a Google account that is not registered in your DB:

In Sign In flow: show “Account does not exist. Please sign up first.”

In Sign Up flow: create a new user.

Security:

No storing Google client secret on frontend.

Google token is converted into your normal JWT for your app session.

Non‑functional:

UX should show a proper error if Google login fails or user cancels.

Works on localhost and on your production domain.